    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d865">

                <pb facs="0750" n="741" xml:id="pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856D.01/38</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Netherland Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Loudon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2693</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-14">May 14, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm the message
                    which I have communicated by telephone to Mr. Berle, the Assistant Secretary of
                    State, that I am in receipt of a telegram from the Netherlands Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs, worded: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“We have absolute conviction that no alteration in political or legal
                            status Netherlands East or West Indies is contemplated by Allies and we
                            also feel confident about Japan.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Loudon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
